9 #edb/ref 1069 "q-38006" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323969 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323969 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the transformation $T:[\\begin{aligned}w \\\\ x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}w-x+2y-z \\\\ x-y-z \\\\ 4w-y+z \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ find its rank." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323969 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cf501bcf-1b6e-5d01-99b4-4fd3685ab11a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323969 #edb/ref 1074 "First, the standard matrix of $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Im}(T))=\\text{rank}(T).$ \n\nSo, we need to find the rank of the matrix $T.$ We reduce $T$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -9 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-4{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $T$ has $3$ pivot columns, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=3.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324177 #edb/ref 1080 "-7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324177 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324177 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "176ffe83-2e48-5777-a382-a57194485053" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324212 #edb/ref 1080 "11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324212 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324212 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1c8a1483-7aea-506a-a4fc-1ccec710489d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324350 #edb/ref 1080 "b\\notin \\text