592186326408 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326408 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186326169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326408 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326408 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326408 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186326169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326408 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6b0c101e-ff21-5508-82ae-d4d7f94e9697" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326510 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325247 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326510 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326510 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326510 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325345 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326510 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326510 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326510 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326510 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186325311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326510 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a3529463-3bcc-58dc-9826-6090e3740721" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326702 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186326408 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326702 #edb/ref 1069 "q-38625" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326702 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326702 #edb/ref 1071 "The standard matrix $T$ of a linear transformation $T$ and the vector $b\\in {R}^{3}$ are given below. Determine if there exists a vector $x\\in {R}^{3}$ such that $T(x)=b.$\nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ are the components of $x.$  \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -28 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326702 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1956fc0c-8f90-53eb-bc19-ee9b28e0deae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326702 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $T$ is the standard matix of $T,$ we have $\\text{Im}(T)=\\text{Col}(T).$ In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Im}(T),$ we need to check if the equation $Tx=b$ is consistent. \n\nSo, we find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[T\\,|\\,b],$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 4 & -28 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 4 & 26\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 8 & 16\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns (the $1$st and the $2$nd). Hence ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n2{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=-8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-4+2{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-5-2{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the general solution is given by \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5-2{x}_{3} \\\\ -4+2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=1$, we have\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere $T(x)=b.$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-7+(-2)=-9.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326704 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186326322 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326704 #edb/ref 1069 "q-38629" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326704 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326704 #edb/ref 1071 "The linear transformation $T$ and the vector $b\\in {R}^{4}$ are given below. Determine if there exists a vector $x\\in {R}^{4}$ such that $T(x)=b.$\nIn the affirmative case, find the value of $w-x+y,$ where $w,x,y,z$ are the components of $x.$  \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}w \\\\ x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}w-3x-2z \\\\ 2x-2w-4y \\\\ 3w-y-10x-7z \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326704 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "592b6ac1-ddb2-56aa-ae83-1783ef1ea8c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326704 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we write down the standard matrix of $T:$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -10 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSince $T$ is the standard matix of $T,$ we have $\\text{Im}(T)=\\text{Col}(T).$ In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Im}(T),$ we need to check if the equation $Tx=b$ is consistent. \n\nSo, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[T\\,|\\,b]$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -10 & -1 & -7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -4 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{4}){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -4 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the false statement $0=-8.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that  $b\\notin \\text{Im}(T).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348488 #edb/ref 1080 "7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348488 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348488 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "04c01e0e-618d-5506-b9d5-fce990196878" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348860 #edb/ref 1080 "17" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348860 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348860 #edb/ref