igned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Im}(T).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351161 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3ed740eb-f508-5f05-8f3f-7a98f936b4b3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351161 #edb/ref 1074 "The vector $v$ belongs to $\\text{Im}(T)$ if there exists a vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]$ such that $T(u)=v.$ \n\nTherefore, we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}3x+y \\\\ x+2y \\\\ -2x+7y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 8 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+y=9 \\\\ x+2y=8 \\\\ -2x+7y=k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x=8-2y$, which we substitute into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+y & =9 \\\\ 3(8-2y)+y & =9 \\\\ -5y & =-15 \\\\ y & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =8-2y \\\\  & =8-2(3) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=2$ and $y=3$ into the third equation and obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+7y & =k \\\\ -2(2)+7(3) & =k \\\\ k & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $v\\in \\text{Im}(T)$ when $k=17.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363175 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363176 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363175 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140078" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363175 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363175 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the transformation\n $T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x+y \\\\ 4z-2x \\\\ z-4x-3y\\end{aligned}],$ find its rank." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363175 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "337abe4f-5c56-58ff-ad12-408abbd32afc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363175 #edb/ref 1074 "First, the standard matrix of $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Im}(T))=\\text{rank}(T).$ \n\nSo, we need to find the rank of the matrix $T.$ We reduce $T$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $T$ has $3$ pivot columns, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=3.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363176 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363176 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363176 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363176 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363176 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363176 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363176 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363176 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186363177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363176 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d53a1aa4-cef0-536f-a0a5-781c11e47a1f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363177 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363177 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363177 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "83d66d8c-c095-55c5-82e5-156fb6a77fa0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363178 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363178 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363178 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "69b89807-97fa-57a7-88d2-88b07ce8c2a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363179 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363179 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363179 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid