\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{4}{3}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns (the $1$st and the $2$nd). Hence ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-9\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-3-{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-1-{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the general solution is given by \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1-{x}_{3} \\\\ -3-{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=2$, we have\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $T(x)=b.$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-3-(-5)=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364126 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364126 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364126 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364129 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364126 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364130 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364126 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364126 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364126 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364126 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186364128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364126 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "59e5ee21-2892-5089-bfdc-97a15df07f35" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364127 #edb/ref 1080 "b\\notin \\text{Im}(T)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364127 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364127 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "03e68c41-7d11-5667-be88-8b3f622f7f5e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364128 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364128 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364128 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e6138bdc-ad92-5fb3-9c42-e886a9